# Lecture 11G

## UPGMA Practice: Extension Problem

## Chapter 11

## Dr. Neil Voss

## November 17, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Build a second six-gene UPGMA tree independently.
- Update distances using all original pairs across clusters.
- Keep fractional cluster averages until the final calculation.
- Check node heights and every branch length.

=== layout: subsection

# Plan Your Steps

=== layout: one-panel

# At Each Step

@body

1. Find the smallest distance and join those clusters.
2. Calculate the new node height: distance / 2.
3. Update the matrix using the original gene-pair distances.
4. Draw branches: parent height - child height.
5. Repeat until all six genes are in one tree.

@notes

Pause for group discussion before showing each answer.

=== layout: one-panel

# Follow the Join Colors

@body

- [*Join 1*]{color=#D40000}
- [*Join 2*]{color=#6C6C00}
- [*Join 3*]{color=#00775F}
- [*Join 4*]{color=#0067CC}
- [*Join 5*]{color=#CC0066}

New branches use the current join color. Earlier branches keep their colors.



